## Incorporated public-domain artwork — not licensed by Telos

Some plates in the fishing guide are works of the United States Fish and
Wildlife Service or other United States federal agencies. As works prepared by
officers or employees of the U.S. Government as part of their official duties,
they are not subject to copyright protection in the United States (17 U.S.C.
§ 105) and are in the public domain. Telos claims no rights in them, and the
CC BY 4.0 license above does not extend to them. Each such plate is credited
individually in `CREDITS.md` and in the caption on the page where it appears.

## No warranty of fitness

The fishing guide is a field reference, not a statement of law: fishing
regulations change and only the Wisconsin Department of Natural Resources
publishes the current rules. The electricity curriculum describes procedures
involving lethal voltages. Both are provided without warranty of any kind, and
the reader assumes full responsibility for verifying regulations and for their
own safety and the safety of others.
